<title>USA: US cash ammonia underpinned by N. Orleans downtime.</title>
<headline>US cash ammonia underpinned by N. Orleans downtime.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. cash ammonia prices were holding up on Wednesday, underpinned by some downtime at New Orleans production facilities despite weakness in the world market. Cash sources noted reports of trade at lower prices late last week but said only 600 tons had traded and the price did not represent that of a full barge load.</p>
<p>DAP prices were narrowly mixed.</p>
<p>				Dlrs/short ton     Chg from Monday</p>
<p>DAP central Fla	   178-180		  up 1.00-unch</p>
<p>DAP central La Gulf     186-188		    dn 2.00</p>
<p>Ammonia/La Gulf	   220-225			nc</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
